2:T7cb,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a property dispute take to resolve in Roorkee civil court? (जमीन विवाद सुलझाने में कितना समय लगता है?)","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Civil property suits involve title verification, framing of issues, witness evidence, and final arguments. While full trials take time, urgent stay orders (Temporary Injunction Order 39 CPC) to stop illegal construction or sale can be obtained in initial court hearings."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can an owner prevent illegal encroachment or unauthorized sale of land?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An owner can file a civil suit for Permanent Injunction along with an application for Temporary Stay under Order 39 Rules 1 & 2 CPC in Civil Court to prohibit the opposite party from entering or selling the land."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the procedure for ancestral property partition among legal heirs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"If family co-owners cannot agree on an informal split, a civil suit for Partition and Separate Possession is filed in the Civil Court to determine each legal heir’s share according to personal succession laws."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which court hears revenue land mutation and boundary disputes in Haridwar district?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Agricultural land revenue matters, khatauni mutation disputes, and boundary demarcations (Paimaish) fall under the jurisdiction of Revenue Courts (Tehsildar, SDM Court, and Collector Court)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What documents are essential for instituting a civil property suit?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Crucial documents include registered sale deeds, chain of previous title deeds, Khatauni / Khasra revenue extracts, municipal tax receipts, site maps, and photographs of possession."}}]}0:{"buildId":"FH8UeKfY7251wkI4fw6lu","rsc":["$","$1","c",{"childre